.page lsusb 1 list USB devices

# SYNOPSIS
*lsusb*

# DESCRIPTION
`lsusb` prints `/proc/usb`, the list of USB devices the kernel has enumerated: one line per device with its port, vendor and product ids, name, speed and the driver that took it (`hid-keyboard`, `hid-mouse`, `hub`, `usb-storage`, or `none`), and one indented line per interface. A USB stick shows `driver usb-storage`; a device that speaks only UAS (interface protocol 62) shows `driver none` and is not used.

For what the mass storage driver makes of a stick (its state, its disk name, error counters), read `/proc/usbstorage`.

If the kernel has no USB support it says `no USB subsystem (no /proc/usb)` and exits with status 1.

# SEE ALSO
lspci(1), lsblk(1), dmesg(1)
